 This question can be solved using the following steps:
 moments required to clear the shelter = total number of puppies to be adopted / number of puppies adopted per day. So, number of moments required = 43 (original puppies + additional puppies) / 8 ... solve for this expression:
\boxed{\frac{43}{8} = 5.375}

 This represents how many "days" are necessary, assuming other puppies are not coming into the shelter and being adopted at the same rate. However, since it is impossible to have a fraction of a day, it would be wrong to round this answer down. Instead, we should round up to the nearest whole number, since it is better to have more time (an extra day) than to not have enough time (not adopting all puppies in the calculated time). Therefore, the final answer is:
\boxed{6}

 So, it would take 6 days for all of the puppies to be adopted if the current adoption rate continues at 8 puppies per day and no new puppies are added.

